From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:35:58 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 65/70] net: wireless: samsung: scsc: build the Wi-Fi driver on
 6.18

Add Kconfig/Makefile for the station-mode subset and adapt the imported
4.14 sources to 6.18:

- cfg80211: small adapters for the ops whose prototypes changed
  (wireless_dev, MLO link_id, radio_idx, cfg80211_ap_update, rx_addr);
  the empty mgmt_frame_register op is dropped; roam info uses links[0];
  ch_switch_notify gets link 0; new_sta/del_sta take the wireless_dev.
- read-only dev_addr: eth_hw_addr_set(); add_vif/mlme_start take const
  addresses.
- timers (timer_delete*, timer_container_of), netif_rx, timespec64,
  proc_ops/pde_data, class_create without owner, <linux/if_arp.h>.
- files by bare name through the firmware loader (6.11+ refuses ".."):
  the regulatory database; the EFS MAC-file fallback (a ".." request,
  and a kernel read of EFS) is removed. With no module/sysfs/mac.txt
  address, a random locally administered MAC replaces the 4.14 SoC-UID
  derivation (no exynos_soc_info on 6.18).
- the driver's own RPS map rewrite (netdev internals) becomes a no-op;
  RPS is configured from userspace on current kernels.
- no VFS-internal namespace import.
- SLSI_IS_VIF_INDEX_MHS_DUALSTA is false without Wi-Fi sharing.

Samsung's private-command code only builds with WES/NCHO, so that option
is a hidden always-on symbol; the commands are unreachable on 6.18
(SIOCDEVPRIVATE goes to ndo_siocdevprivate, not implemented), all NCHO
modes stay 0 and behave as a non-NCHO build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I530fa0689e2041ed9ea47054ec9662ca8a4c61bd
